{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head fd75637eb4e9169f7937d1ec8bdddbb6a31849b5, tree 04cd7584658e2e0874344b391cb2aeb045a88c29, on builder/rs1-on-published-main-20261115, all 18 artifacts, for request 7d3313e7 under my promise 1123f1ba and standing da772676. This verdict names both implementations: RS-1 (request e3dff17f, promise 3e6b93a4, report ea9c5c3d, the RS-1 note, primary) and LS-2 (request 686c7da2, promise fb957330, report d295a200, the LS-2 note). `gs review --prepare` resolved both bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. I read the head from the shared object store. The branch is not on origin.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `examples/lending/definition.ts` and `definition.json`. A `reservation` gains the fixed party `holder` and the final state `released`. `reserve` sets `holder` to the signer. It keeps the `tool-day-taken` guard and adds a `count` guard: at most one other `held` reservation whose `holder` is the signer, so a member holds at most two live reservations. `release` needs `lending.member`, a `held` reservation and the signer as its `holder`. `release-by-staff` needs `lending.staff` and a `held` reservation. Both move the reservation to `released` and change nothing else. `max: 8`, the `lapse` rule, the opaque day labels and the absence of a longest `until` stay as they were.\n- The authorities. A member can release only a reservation that names them as `holder`. Staff can release any held reservation, under a grant that holds `lending.staff` alone. Neither act touches the tool, so a release cannot change a `thing`. A released or lapsed reservation is final, so no act brings it back.\n- `packages/define/src/package.ts`. `manifest` takes an optional `capabilities` list. When the list is absent, the old derivation from the definition's capabilities runs unchanged, so Counter and Grow keep their bytes. When it is present, it replaces the derived list. `examples/lending/package.ts` now passes the `publication-paths@1` declaration through that option instead of spreading over the result. The new package case checks both answers.\n- The Lending identifiers. Entry, definitions, semantic and presentation all change, as a new definition requires. The pin in `pin.ts` equals the new entry. Lending stays at the open 0.4.0, and no file under `releases/` changes, so neither signed 0.3.0 packet moves. Counter and Grow identifiers do not change. `application-examples.test.ts` now expects 38 steps with replay through 15.\n- `examples/lending/story.ts` and the definition test. Each one reserves two slots, refuses a third, refuses a release by a non-holder with no new entry, releases by the holder, lets another member take the freed slot, releases by staff, and checks that the tool is unchanged and that replay equals state.\n- LS-2, `scripts/celld-smoke.mjs`. A failure at the `install` stage computes one label from the CLI exit code and first line, chosen from 14 fixed labels, and keeps only that label. The error never stores the CLI lines. `celldSmokeDetail` returns a label only for the `install` stage and only when the label is in the fixed map, and `scripts/test-celld-proxy.mjs` adds that one field. The new test cases put a sentinel in every dynamic part of each form and in the error's message, stack and cause, and show that the projection never contains it.\n- Both notes. The RS-1 note keeps the earlier compiler and producer failures. The LS-2 note states that the old Linux install cause is still unknown.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main fb7877d9 is an ancestor. The 18 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only fb7877d9 fd75637e`. From the gated head 3bedd5c8 to this head only the two notes change.\n- Gate, END 54c0f829. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-rs1-ls2-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 a8948344…, as the request states. It names head 3bedd5c8 and tree 87c399cc with 0 changed files. Kernel, Node 204, Counting 56, Plain 4860 with 1 skipped and Native 1136 with 2 skipped all passed, and its last line is \"gate passed\". Scale selected nothing, so no Scale case ran. The `controls` directory holds the three control records: `rs1-holder`, `rs1-live-bound` and `ls2`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 11 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The release uses the existing `transition` form with state and party guards. The limit of two uses the existing `count` guard over `held` reservations. The `manifest` option replaces the hand-written spread that my review fb722a09 named, and its default keeps every other package unchanged. LS-2 selects a public label from a fixed list instead of passing CLI text.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The holder release checks the signer against the fixed `holder` party, so one member cannot end another member's hold. The staff release needs `lending.staff`. The two-hold limit closes the fact from review fb722a09, where one member could hold all eight reservations. Staff can now free any slot.\n- LS-2 keeps the private boundary. Only a fixed label crosses into the proxy's error line, and a label that is not in the map projects as nothing.\n\nOne fact for a later screen: the third `reserve` fails the `count` guard with the generic reason `guard-failed`, and the Lending annotations show \"That thing cannot be cancelled now.\" for that reason on `reserve`. No screen offers `reserve` at this head, so no member sees those words yet. A screen that offers `reserve` needs its own words for the limit.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The head removes the `package.ts` spread that copied the capability by hand.\n\nQualifications that stand: the earlier RS-1 compiler and producer failures stay in the note. The gate ran no Scale case, and the scope-stories timings stay partial. The LS-2 change adds diagnostics only. The old Linux install cause is unknown, and no \"Local Worker smoke\" pass is claimed. No browser, hosted install, provider, physical-device, signed release or formal-model result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea9c5c3d534c7a320738802014a2f06879220cd6","binding":"assigned","head":"fd75637eb4e9169f7937d1ec8bdddbb6a31849b5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1123f1ba8dee7fb10f76c244685260a091b5947d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3e6b93a4b8d31741bcfced1e0515d76e35116142\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb957330a5a56ec009174a0eef3e54b6b7c0a86d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1123f1ba8dee7fb10f76c244685260a091b5947d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}